On Sun, 29 Jan 2006, bob wrote:
> So, for those gurus out there who can hdlp us stumbling klutz, direction 
> impaired geeks who want X on the NetBSD desk top .... is there some way to 
> get this X capability in the basic build of NetBSD Alpha?

I think that would be nice. Until the alpha- and X-enclued people join in, 
I've managed to get a few bits of information:

0) Apparently even NetBSD-current doesn't build XFree86 for the alpha,
    only soem non-XFree-based servers (XdecSomething, XalphaOtherthing)
1) First step would be to get XFree built (preferably as part of the
    'build.sh' build)
2) If that is built and installed into the build.sh destdir(!), then
    it needs to be included into the release sets.

The patch below tries this. If someone wants to give it a try and post 
results, that would be useful, preferably against NetBSD-current sources.

I guess someone may look at integrating the caseydoodle code into xsrc, 
but that'll not be me.

Let me say that I'm not happy about the state of things, and that I'd love 
the current situation to get fixed.


  - Hubert

