It is 166MHz with 128MB.  Full dmesg is attached.
  
The sysdisk is an IBM 4GB SCSI.  No other peripherals -- almost
no room for other peripherals.  ;-)
  
I can't really speak too firmly on the quality of the hardware since
this machine was a "rescue" -- I've never run it in production.  I
did replace the cooling fan with something a little stronger, and it
seems to be reasonably solid.

I installed 1.6.2 on it a while ago, and haven't really used it much.
  
The Multia is located in Sunnyvale, California, USA.  I estimate it
would cost around $30 to ship it inside the USA; I'm not sure it's
worth it to ship outside USA, but if someone is truly desparate to
have it and willing to pay the extra expense, I'll send it overseas.
  
Cheers,
sr.
